    "finalText": "Done. Container `onlycli-demo` removed; `openapi.yaml` and `server.go` untouched.\n\n**Install method**\n- Single ephemeral `golang:1.24-bookworm` (linux/arm64) container.\n- Downloaded the upstream v0.2.0 linux/arm64 release tarball, verified it with `checksums.txt` (`sha256sum -c`), extracted, and installed to `/usr/local/bin/onlycli`.\n- `onlycli version` confirmed `0.2.0` (commit `84217179091d...`, built `2026-03-27`).\n\n**Execution path**\n- `onlycli generate --spec openapi.yaml --name demo-cli --out ./demo-cli` → 1 group (`api`), 1 command (`get-echo`).\n- `cd demo-cli && go mod tidy && go build -o demo-cli .`\n- `go run server.go` in `/work`, served on `127.0.0.1:18080`.\n- Smoke: `cd demo-cli && ./demo-cli api get-echo --id 42 --format json`\n\n**Smoke output**\n```json\n{\"id\":\"42\",\"message\":\"ok\"}\n```\n\n**Artifacts**\n- `out/demo-cli/` (generated project + built `demo-cli` binary)\n- `out/result.json` (all required fields)\n\n**Friction**\n- `bash -lc` in the Go image resets PATH and hides `/usr/local/go/bin`; used `bash -c` instead.\n- The spec has no tags, so the command is grouped under `api`; `operationId: getEcho` becomes `get-echo`.\n- Generated CLI defaulted to bearer auth (auto-detected) but the mock server needs no token, so it worked unauthenticated."
