    "finalText": "Completed successfully.\n\n**Install method**\n- Used `golang:1.24-bookworm` in one Docker container, never the host.\n- Downloaded the upstream `onlycli_0.2.0_linux_arm64.tar.gz` release asset.\n- Verified SHA-256 against upstream `checksums.txt`, then installed the `onlycli` binary to `/usr/local/bin`.\n- Confirmed: `onlycli version 0.2.0`.\n\n**Execution path**\n- Generated project: `onlycli generate --spec openapi.yaml --name demo-cli --out ./demo-cli`\n- Built: `cd demo-cli && go mod tidy && go build -o demo-cli .`\n- Started `server.go` on `127.0.0.1:18080` inside the same container.\n- Smoke command:\n  ```bash\n  ./demo-cli api get-echo --id 42 --format json\n  ```\n- Smoke output:\n  ```json\n  {\"id\":\"42\",\"message\":\"ok\"}\n  ```\n\n**Artifacts**\n- Generated project and binary: `out/demo-cli/`\n- Built binary: `out/demo-cli/demo-cli`\n- Result file: `out/result.json`\n\nThe container was removed after copying artifacts. `openapi.yaml` and `server.go` were not modified.\n\n**Friction**\n- The spec has no tags, so the generated operation was placed under a generic `api` group.\n- The release tarball was required to pin exactly v0.2.0, since the README’s `go install ...@latest` does not guarantee that version.\n- `go mod tidy` required network access to fetch generated dependencies.\n- The generated project defaults its module path to `github.com/demo-cli/demo-cli-cli`, which is redundant but harmless."
